    "source": "MeSH_SCAN_SN.txt",
    "description": "MeSH-heading-based keyword taxonomy, curated from the actual meshHeadingList values found on papers in Social Cognitive and Affective Neuroscience (SCAN) and Social Neuroscience via the Europe PMC core API. Entries here have a single 'mesh_terms' list matched by EXACT set membership against a paper's own indexed MeSH descriptor names (no 'search_terms'/'stems' split, no stemmer -- MeSH is already a controlled vocabulary, so there is nothing to stem). 'schema_topics'/'schema_modality' map an entry onto data/schema.json's enums; an empty list means no clean enum match, so hits are stored under 'tags' instead. This file is self-contained (journals + topics + methods) so the MeSH pipeline (mesh_search_europepmc.py / mesh_extract_candidate.py / mesh_run_pipeline.py) has no dependency on keywords.json or the free-text pipeline. Excluded from the source vocabulary: MEDLINE checktags (Humans, Animals, Male, Female, Adult, Child, Aged, Infant, ...), generic statistical/design terms present on nearly every paper (Regression Analysis, Reproducibility of Results, Surveys and Questionnaires, Neuropsychological Tests, Photic/Acoustic Stimulation, ...), pure brain-anatomy terms with no topic/method meaning alone (Prefrontal Cortex, Amygdala, Hippocampus, Brain, Brain Mapping, ...) -- this is the 'brain regions' noise flagged in SCRAPING_NOTE.md -- and country/institution/demographic-group/species terms (Canada, White People, Students, Macaca mulatta, ...). Also confirmed by spot-checking Europe PMC: PET, TMS, tDCS, DTI and iEEG (all present in keywords.json's free-text methods list) have combined hit counts of 0-1 across SCAN + Social Neuroscience's MeSH indexing, so they are deliberately omitted from schema_modality methods here rather than carried over unverified."
  },
